{
  "title": "The Dual Agent Harness",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "0b08baad57beac41",
      "text": "# The Dual Agent Harness ⚔️🧙\n\nA verification harness for AI-agent work: one agent proposes, a second independently proves, and the tests that decide are derived by hashing the proposal together with a secret the proposer never sees — so it cannot grind them."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "25291e31dde16033",
      "text": "An agent that proposes a change and then checks its own change will pass — not because it cheats, but because the check it invents is the check its change was built to survive. The harness names that output a **mirage**: it passes the author's probe and fails the real gate. Between the proposer (soulbae 🧙) and the prover (soulbis ⚔️) sits **the Gap ⿻**, and above them both is **the First Person 😊**, who alone opens the door to anything outward-facing."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "33578c7cd2e05cda",
      "text": "On the ring of integers mod 64 the inscription is a theorem: negation composed with complement is the successor — two *different* inversions, held apart, produce the step forward. A proposer checked by a copy of itself is an identity operation."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "ac130b426c45b982",
      "text": "## Where the skeleton went\n\nFifteen real embodiments wear this skeleton — quantum circuits, ZK constraint systems, research pipelines, consent agreements, an acceptance registry with an external counterparty, a literature review run against an adversary, and one deliberate failure kept on purpose. The repo's HARNESS_PATHS.md is the map; this wall's sibling site [[field-guide workshop]] shows the runnable spar in full."
    },
    {
      "type": "reference",
      "site": "field-guide.localhost",
      "slug": "field-guide-workshop",
      "title": "field-guide workshop",
      "text": "The spar: compress a field guide while a hash-drawn comprehension census must stay a full pass.",
      "id": "1a54c91cc1377f9f"
    },
